tion and Dietetics: A Comprehensive Review of Current Research#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#Artificial Intelligence in Nutrition and Dietetics: A Comprehensive Review of Current Research#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42],"#Artificial Intelligence in Nutrition and Dietetics: A Comprehensive Review of Current Research#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)#{1}":[42,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/TI4JB657","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WER5XM88?page=1&annotation=XQ3ADSQ5","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WER5XM88?page=1&annotation=YIZWCIMD","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WER5XM88?page=1&annotation=DRW4VZRK","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 14","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WER5XM88?page=14&annotation=9NXYNTRW","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 14","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WER5XM88?page=14&annotation=XYTE2IAV","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 14","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WER5XM88?page=14&annotation=YQ2I6EGJ","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 15","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WER5XM88?page=15&annotation=LAQ4Y2JP","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 12","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WER5XM88?page=12&annotation=6N788JGY","line":42},{"title":"Sayfa 12","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/WER5XM88?page=12&annotation=E3JCFK6A","line":42}],"metadata":{"Title":"Artificial Intelligence in Nutrition and Dietetics: A Comprehensive Review of Current Research","Authors":"Gabriela Georgieva Panayotova","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.3390/healthcare13202579","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"A systematic literature search was conducted across PubMed, Scopus, Web of Science, and Google Scholar for peer-reviewed publications from January 2020 to July 2025. The search included studies involving AI applications in nutrition, dietetics, or public health nutrition.  Articles were screened based on predefined inclusion and exclusion criteria. Thematic analysis grouped findings into six categories: dietary assessment, personalized nutrition and chronic disease management, generative AI and conversational agents, global/public health nutrition, sensory science and food innovation, and ethical and professional considerati","Findings":"AI-driven systems show strong potential for improving dietary tracking accuracy, generating personalized diet recommendations, and supporting disease-specific nutrition management. Chatbots and large language models (LLMs) are increasingly used for education and support. Despite this progress, challenges remain regarding model transparency, ethical use of health data, limited generalizability across diverse populations, and underrepresentation of low-resource settin","Conclusions":"However, responsible development, ethical oversight, and inclusive validation across populations are essential to ensure equitable and safe integration into clinical and public health practice.Persistent challenges include algorithmic bias, privacy and security, explainability, and the need for standardized validation and external, multi-site evaluatioIn practice, AI should augment—not replace—dietitians; in policy, governance for interoperability, data protection, and transparent reporting remains essential to safe, equitable adoption.Based on this review’s results, AI is most mature in image-based dietary assessment, personalized coaching/decision support for weight, diabetes, and cardiometabolic riskand conversational education; these tools show moderate-to-strong accuracy in controlled studies and can improve self-monitoring and engagement.","Limitations":"Many studies use inconsistent metrics, making cross-comparison difficuMost models trained on Western, high-income populations; poor adaptation to diverse diets","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"991euj","at":1774939749120},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/panayotovaArtificialIntelligenceNutrition2025a.md"},
